{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774301408,"nonce":"HelRBeGbfJMjKkEVidH/fgydcZs=","message":"## Implementation Spec: Figure Gallery Tab\n\n### Architecture Decision\nFigures is a **new top-level tab** in BottomShelf (alongside Training, Console, Analysis, Trajectories, Statistics). Rationale: figures are a distinct browsable artifact collection, not a subsection of the Analysis dashboard placeholder. The gallery workflow (browse/filter/view) is self-contained.\n\n### Components\n- **FigureGalleryPanel** — main panel with filter bar (top), gallery grid (main area), and FigureViewer overlay\n- **FigureCard** — thumbnail card showing identifier, figure_type badge, perturbation info, experiment name, date, and available formats\n- **FigureViewer** — full overlay (within panel, not modal) with Plotly.js rendering for JSON figures, image display for png/svg/webp, iframe for HTML. Includes download links for all available formats. Closes on ESC or X button.\n\n### Data Flow\n- **figureAPI.ts** — API client wrapping `/api/figures`, `/api/figures/evaluations`, `/api/figures/{hash}`, `/api/figures/{hash}/file`\n- **useFigures.ts** — hook managing filter state, pagination (24 per page), figure list fetching, and viewer state (detail + file loading). No Zustand store — hook-local state is sufficient since this tab has no cross-component state needs.\n- Filter options (evaluations, experiment names) loaded from `/api/figures/evaluations`. Figure types and perturbation types derived from current result set.\n\n### UI Patterns\n- Follows TrajectoryPanel/StatisticsPanel layout: top filter bar with selects and pill buttons, main scrollable content, overlay states for loading/error/empty\n- Reuses the same Tailwind classes: `rounded-xl border border-slate-100 bg-slate-50/70` cards, `text-brand-*` accent colors, `Loader2` spinner, ChevronLeft/Right pagination\n- Gallery uses CSS grid with `grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr))]` for responsive layout\n- Plotly.js imported dynamically to avoid adding 3MB to initial bundle\n\n### Dependencies\n- Added `plotly.js-dist-min` (minified Plotly.js distribution, ~1MB)\n- Added `src/plotly.d.ts` for TypeScript declarations","files":null}]}